From: TG5050 downstream reconstruction
Subject: [PATCH] drm: sunxi: restore stock DE350 RCQ AHB trigger ordering

The shipping TG5050 5.15.147 Image calls de_top_update_force_by_ahb()
in sunxi_de_atomic_flush() after optional automatic frequency calculation
and before the RCQ timer/direct request branch. The public Tina BSP has
the exact call commented out.

Keep this distinct from the old post-resume force-flush experiment and
from the remaining DE-top DFS/RCQ-dispatch reconstruction. It restores
only the direct, instruction-verified call ordering on the normal RCQ
path; it does not affect disabled, force-sentinel, double-buffer, or
non-RCQ paths.

Stock evidence: vendor-kernel-5.15.147.Image SHA-256
51b4b92047f82b7c52cf67e445618cc79e0863ee737359a5644b959d1dd9ec7b;
sunxi_de_atomic_flush VA 0xffffffc008832500 calls
de_top_update_force_by_ahb at 0xffffffc0088326a0.

See build/vendor-patch-reconstruction/de-flush.md and
packaging/rpm/bsp-custom/VENDOR-RECONSTRUCTION.md.

--- a/drivers/drm/sunxi_device/hardware/lowlevel_de/sunxi_de.c
+++ b/drivers/drm/sunxi_device/hardware/lowlevel_de/sunxi_de.c
@@ -728,7 +728,7 @@
 
 		if (engine->de_devfreq_auto)
 			sunxi_de_auto_calc_freq_and_apply(engine->display_out);
-		// de_top_update_force_by_ahb(engine->top_hdl);
+		de_top_update_force_by_ahb(engine->top_hdl);
 
 		if (engine->match_data->rcq_wait_line)
 			rcq_update_timer_start(hwde);
